WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:06.520
Hey Team, it’s Charlie and Fox just announced
that the Deadpool Movie is back on.

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:12.920
They have a date, this right here 2/12/2016,
they have a director and they have an actor.

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:15.169
What fine actor have they chosen?

00:00:15.169 --> 00:00:18.730
You guessed it, Ryan Reynolds is still attached
as is director Tim Miller.

00:00:18.730 --> 00:00:23.820
The two were the ones originally working on
the film back when Fox first put it into development

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:25.670
back in 2011.

00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:29.500
Here are the Top 8 awesome things that we
can all be excited about:

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:33.610
Number 8 - The leaked test footage is a better
trailer than a real trailer ever could be.

00:00:33.610 --> 00:00:36.309
And it came at the right time.

00:00:36.309 --> 00:00:39.309
Deadpool is being released in the winter,
but it’s a comic book movie.

00:00:39.309 --> 00:00:42.629
Awareness and engagement for those types of
movies peaks during the summer.

00:00:42.629 --> 00:00:44.399
Particularly around Comic Con.

00:00:44.399 --> 00:00:48.340
We can thank all the Hall H exclusives and
big reveals studios hold for that weekend.

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:52.559
It just trains people to attach themselves
to their computers and cell phones waiting

00:00:52.559 --> 00:00:53.559
for updates.

00:00:53.559 --> 00:00:58.499
Low and behold, some unofficial but very authentic
seeming Deadpool test footage starts getting

00:00:58.499 --> 00:00:59.890
passed around.

00:00:59.890 --> 00:01:04.770
Fox takes it down, guaranteeing it’s authenticity
and heightening demand.

00:01:04.770 --> 00:01:09.410
Over the comic con weekend the footage gets
taken down and reuploaded several times and

00:01:09.410 --> 00:01:15.320
Rhett Reese, the writer of the current Deadpool
movie script launches a twitter campaign.

00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:19.570
Retweet if you would buy a ticket to a deadpool
movie.

00:01:19.570 --> 00:01:24.110
Comic Book Creators like Bendis, Fraction
and Rob Liefeld as well as other big celebrities

00:01:24.110 --> 00:01:27.420
throw their support in via twitter and facebook.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:30.060
And everything goes quiet near the end of
August.

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:34.210
Probably not though, because Fox executives
probably saw what was happening early on and

00:01:34.210 --> 00:01:35.390
decided to move forward.

00:01:35.390 --> 00:01:39.830
It just took this long for them to announce
the movie because contracts needed to be signed.

00:01:39.830 --> 00:01:45.700
If you ever wonder why Marvel doesn’t announce
stuff more often, it’s because actors, writers

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:48.460
and directors haven’t signed contracts yet.

00:01:48.460 --> 00:01:53.200
Movie studios only make official announcements
when everyone involved is legally bound to

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:55.950
complete the movie.

00:01:55.950 --> 00:02:00.850
Number 7 - Even though the test footage was
largely digital effects, the movie will mostly

00:02:00.850 --> 00:02:03.200
be live action.

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:10.890
There are a lot of ways digital effects can
help a Deadpool story, mostly talking severed

00:02:10.890 --> 00:02:16.450
heads, but the current movie culture is returning
to the familiarity of practical effects.

00:02:16.450 --> 00:02:19.840
That means building things in real life instead
of in the computer.

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:25.489
You may have noticed JJ Abrams trolling Zack
Snyder with this Millenium Falcon reveal.

00:02:25.489 --> 00:02:31.099
Underneath you can see the old Christopher
Nolan tumbler attached in a very empire strikes

00:02:31.099 --> 00:02:34.159
back way.

00:02:34.159 --> 00:02:41.269
Abrams, rather than build everything on a
green screen chose to build most of the large

00:02:41.269 --> 00:02:42.680
sets, aliens and vehicles.

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:45.130
A very wise choice in my opinion.

00:02:45.130 --> 00:02:53.510
Marvel still uses a lot of digital effects
for their movies, but a lot of times the choice

00:02:53.510 --> 00:02:59.230
of CG versus practical effects just comes
down to budget and time.

00:02:59.230 --> 00:03:03.999
We know the movie is scheduled for release
February 2016 which gives them till next summer

00:03:03.999 --> 00:03:05.340
to shoot the film.

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:11.719
For quick turnover movies like Avengers and
Deadpool they can get a movie out within 8

00:03:11.719 --> 00:03:13.280
months of shooting the actors.

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:16.689
Again, that window, also very dependent on
Budget.

00:03:16.689 --> 00:03:21.060
Bigger Budgets means you can hire more post
production people to get your movie out faster.

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:25.630
Given Ryan Reynolds involvement and it being
an X-Men Franchise movie I’d guess their

00:03:25.630 --> 00:03:33.560
budget will be between 60 and 80 million dollars.

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:39.970
Maybe more if FOX thinks it’s a guaranteed
hit.

00:03:39.970 --> 00:03:44.599
Number 6 - The Director Tim Miller isn’t
just the original director attached to the

00:03:44.599 --> 00:03:45.599
project.

00:03:45.599 --> 00:03:51.939
He’s the guy at Blur Studios who leaked
the test footage before comic con this year.

00:03:51.939 --> 00:03:57.379
Arguably the first in a series of events that
led Fox to pulling the movie out of mothballs.

00:03:57.379 --> 00:04:01.540
Blur Studios are the people Fox hired back
in 2011 to develop the project.

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:04.999
They’re primarily known as a visual effects
studio.

00:04:04.999 --> 00:04:07.659
Miller himself has been very lucky.

00:04:07.659 --> 00:04:12.409
Had the public response not been so great,
FOX could have sued him into oblivion for

00:04:12.409 --> 00:04:14.059
leaking the Deadpool footage.

00:04:14.059 --> 00:04:19.479
Fox is owned by Rupert Murdoch, he’s every
bit as litigious as Mr Burns on the Simpsons.

00:04:19.479 --> 00:04:23.720
Clearly if he was willing to risk being thrown
in a deep dark hole, he must really be passionate

00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:28.129
about the movie, which is key and makes me
optimistic that he’ll do a good job.

00:04:28.129 --> 00:04:32.740
There’s a lot more involved in making a
good movie than just the director.

00:04:32.740 --> 00:04:36.449
But he’s the one guy everyone working on
the movie goes to for answers.

00:04:36.449 --> 00:04:40.970
That’s why a lot of movie directors get
labeled as glorified traffic cops.

00:04:40.970 --> 00:04:45.300
That’s kind of pejorative though, so if
you know any directors in real life and you

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:49.070
call them that, they’ll probably punch you
in the face.

00:04:49.070 --> 00:04:52.610
Number 5 - Ryan Reynolds is still attached
to star

00:04:52.610 --> 00:04:57.800
He’s not currently under contract but still
remains committed to the project.

00:04:57.800 --> 00:05:02.229
Shooting dates and making him official just
requires working out the schedule.

00:05:02.229 --> 00:05:06.759
Right now Reynolds has two movies he’s committed
to in addition to Deadpool, all three of them

00:05:06.759 --> 00:05:12.060
are scheduled for release in 2016, which means
next year, they’ll all be filming.

00:05:12.060 --> 00:05:19.500
One of those movies is Croods 2, which will
only require voice-over work and isn’t half

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:23.030
as demanding on his time as a live action
movie with a lot of other actors on screen

00:05:23.030 --> 00:05:24.030
at the same time.

00:05:24.030 --> 00:05:27.240
So it’s totally possible for them to shoot
the movie with him.

00:05:27.240 --> 00:05:33.139
If they ran into big problems, what they might
do is shoot any footage of him without the

00:05:33.139 --> 00:05:34.240
mask on if they needed to.

00:05:34.240 --> 00:05:35.910
And then for the remainder of the film.

00:05:35.910 --> 00:05:39.780
Just use a body double and have him provide
the dialogue when his schedule permitted.

00:05:39.780 --> 00:05:43.259
It’s a lot easier to shoot a movie if you
don’t actually need your a-list actor on

00:05:43.259 --> 00:05:45.440
set all the time.

00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:49.750
And because Wade Wilson pretty much wears
the mask full time, if they wanted.

00:05:49.750 --> 00:05:54.389
I feel like the fandom wouldn’t care if
he never took the mask off completely.

00:05:54.389 --> 00:05:59.259
Fox’s renewed interest in the project probably
has a lot to do with Reynolds.

00:05:59.259 --> 00:06:03.949
So the chances this movie goes into production
increase exponentially the minute they get

00:06:03.949 --> 00:06:04.990
him under contract.

00:06:04.990 --> 00:06:10.300
Number 4 - They already have a finished script
from the original writer Rhett Reese

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:13.930
No word on whether this is the script that
they’ll shoot with or if they’ll try to

00:06:13.930 --> 00:06:16.360
re-write it.

00:06:16.360 --> 00:06:21.000
But the mere fact they have a finished script
is a huge bonus and add to that, the test

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:23.960
footage everyone saw.

00:06:23.960 --> 00:06:25.610
Was based on parts of Reese’s Script.

00:06:25.610 --> 00:06:35.250
So if you liked the way the test footage played,
you’ll probably enjoy the rest of that story.

00:06:35.250 --> 00:06:39.050
The rest of it is said to include a ton of
equally crazy action sequences.

00:06:39.050 --> 00:06:42.360
And yes, it was written as a very hard R movie.

00:06:42.360 --> 00:06:43.490
Mostly for violence and gore.

00:06:43.490 --> 00:06:48.520
But also lots of foul mouthed wisecracking.

00:06:48.520 --> 00:06:52.930
Number 3 - The Script also features Several
Mutants from the X-Men Universe

00:06:52.930 --> 00:07:01.960
Just to name a few there’s, Wyre, Ajax,
Sluggo, Garrison Kane and Daniel Cudmore’s

00:07:01.960 --> 00:07:02.960
Colossus.

00:07:02.960 --> 00:07:06.750
And Deadpool specific characters like Vanessa
Carlysle and Blind AI.

00:07:06.750 --> 00:07:10.039
Supposedly there’s more but I haven’t
seen the script so this is all just based

00:07:10.039 --> 00:07:12.110
on names that have been released.

00:07:12.110 --> 00:07:15.680
Fox of course owns X-Men, so using mutants
is easy.

00:07:15.680 --> 00:07:20.380
I like the implication that Deadpool will
get to mow down some superheroes and supervillains.

00:07:20.380 --> 00:07:24.969
The character is a mercenary at his core,
so as long as a hit shows up on someone it

00:07:24.969 --> 00:07:26.800
doesn’t matter if they’re good or bad.

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:32.919
No word on who the presumed Big Bad would
be but there’s Sabretooth, Taskmaster, Venom

00:07:32.919 --> 00:07:35.830
and Bullseye and a bunch more.

00:07:35.830 --> 00:07:39.479
Deadpool has had a beef with at least 50 characters
and not all of them were villains .

00:07:39.479 --> 00:07:42.130
A lot of the characters are owned by other
studios.

00:07:42.130 --> 00:07:47.749
So Fox might bend canon a little and use some
other notable big bad from inside the X-Men

00:07:47.749 --> 00:07:48.749
Franchise.

00:07:48.749 --> 00:07:55.099
Or it will be some crazy mind-fuck and deadpool
will end up ordering a hit on himself.

00:07:55.099 --> 00:07:57.310
I don’t think Fox would let the story get
that crazy.

00:07:57.310 --> 00:07:59.540
That would feel more like an episode of Doctor
Who.

00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:03.740
Number 2 - The Official Synopsis For The Character

00:08:03.740 --> 00:08:09.490
Huge Man, armed to the teeth with twin Katanas
and Set Matching Desert Eagle Pistols.

00:08:09.490 --> 00:08:14.360
His Sarcastic Wit and ever-running mouth are
nearly as deadly as his fighting prowess.

00:08:14.360 --> 00:08:17.849
Has a tendency to break the 4th wall and talk
to the audience.

00:08:17.849 --> 00:08:22.800
Boyishly handsome in his youth but is presently
extremely disfigured with scars over face

00:08:22.800 --> 00:08:23.800
and body.

00:08:23.800 --> 00:08:29.090
Let’s be honest, Wolverine is the most popular
character Fox owns, but Deadpool just from

00:08:29.090 --> 00:08:31.360
reading that, is the most fun.

00:08:31.360 --> 00:08:33.380
And you guys will like this last one.

00:08:33.380 --> 00:08:36.270
The Number 1 awesome thing about the Deadpool
Movie is that because it can exist in the

00:08:36.270 --> 00:08:37.270
canon of the X-Men films.

00:08:37.270 --> 00:08:43.560
Deadpool will know that he was a character
in a movie and can make jokes about said movie.

00:08:43.560 --> 00:08:47.640
I think we can all admit that Wolverine Origins
was a little silly with all the screaming

00:08:47.640 --> 00:08:49.470
at the sky and the one-liners.

00:08:49.470 --> 00:08:54.870
But imagine deadpool spending half a movie
making fun of it and making fun of himself

00:08:54.870 --> 00:08:56.079
in the movie.

00:08:56.079 --> 00:09:01.050
His ability to break the fourth wall can at
times be both amazing and incredibly confusing.

00:09:01.050 --> 00:09:10.990
Which is part of why it’s so much fun.

00:09:10.990 --> 00:09:15.800
So big question for you guys, do you think
Deadpool should be able to make jokes about

00:09:15.800 --> 00:09:21.230
Wolverine Origins in the movie and who do
you want the villain to be?

